# Larva pattern data

Pattern data files supply the default (`<name>.prototype.js`) and variant (`<name>.<variant>.js`) data that the pattern server renders and that consuming projects export as JSON.

## Naming and loading

- The server loads `<type>/<name>/<name>.<variant>.js`, with the variant defaulting to `prototype` (`packages/larva/lib/utils/getPatternData.js`). Every `<name>.<variant>.js` in a pattern directory becomes a variant. Any other file name is never loaded.
- CommonJS only. `module.exports = { … }` exports a plain object; variants export the mutated clone (`module.exports = button;`).
- Keys mirror the Twig variables and carry the same escaping suffixes (`newsletter_classes`, `c_tagline_text`, `c_link_url`; see `.agents/rules/larva-twig-templates.md`). Child data sits under the child's snake_case name (`c_title`, `o_email_capture_form`).

## Clone before mutating

Require child data and clone it right away:

```js
const clonedeep = require( 'lodash.clonedeep' );

const c_title_prototype = require( '../../components/c-title/c-title.prototype' );
const c_title = clonedeep( c_title_prototype );
```

- Never mutate a required prototype in place. Node caches modules, so the change would leak into every pattern and page that requires the same prototype.
- Variants start from their own prototype: `const button = clonedeep( require( './button.prototype' ) );`
- Append classes with `+=` and a leading space (`o_card.o_card_classes += ' lrv-u-flex';`). Use plain assignment only to replace.
- Set a child to `false` to suppress it (`c_tagline_terms.c_tagline_text = false;`). The Twig `{% if %}` guard then skips it.
- Placeholder content only: dummy text and `#` URLs. These files are demo and default data, and themes replace the values.

Preferred default: inside `packages/larva-patterns/`, use a relative `require( '../../<type>/<name>/<name>.prototype' )` + `clonedeep` (94 files vs 34 using the package path). In a consuming project's `src/patterns/`, require larva data by package path (`@penskemediacorp/larva-patterns/…`), because the relative layout does not exist there.
`__experimentalCloneWithFallback` (`packages/larva/lib/utils/clonePatternData.js`) lets consuming projects override larva data with their own `src/patterns/` files. Inside larva-patterns, plain `clonedeep( require( … ) )` is the norm.

## Counter-examples

- `const c_title = require( '../../components/c-title/c-title.prototype' ); c_title.c_title_text = 'X';` mutates the shared module.
- `c_button_classes = 'lrv-u-…'` when the intent was to add to the defaults (drops the base classes).
- A file named `newsletter-form.js` or `newsletter.form.data.js`: the server never loads it as a variant.

## New data file workflow

1. Create `<name>.prototype.js` exporting every key the Twig template reads.
2. For each child, require its prototype and `clonedeep` it before changing fields.
3. For a variant, create `<name>.<variant>.js` that clones `./<name>.prototype` and overrides only what differs.
4. Check with `npm run larva` at `/larva/<type>/<name>/<variant>`.

Example: `packages/larva-patterns/modules/newsletter/newsletter.prototype.js`.

